vaporOS nuttx-apps patch: lua-maxccalls

Problem:   Lua allows 200 nested C calls (LUAI_MAXCCALLS) before it raises "C stack
           overflow". NuttX runs Lua in a task with a fixed stack and no guard page, so
           on a small stack (vlua has 24 KB) the 200th level is far past the end of the
           stack: deep pcall/metamethod/callback nesting, or an lpeg pattern nested 300
           deep, silently overwrites the memory below the stack and resets the board.
Evidence:  RP2040-Zero, vlua. /proc/self/stack StackUsed grows 480 bytes per nested
           pcall (depth 20: 11992, depth 30: 16792, stack 24520), so about 45 levels
           fit. A crash record (xd 2003ff00) after an lpeg test showed the stack
           pointer 19 KB below stack_base. NOT shown: that every crash seen in the lpeg
           suite has this cause (one was a bad pointer inside luaH_getshortstr).
Fix:       new INTERPRETERS_LUA_MAXCCALLS (default 200 = upstream behaviour) passed as
           -DLUAI_MAXCCALLS. A board sets it to about stack_size / 500.
           Honoured by Lua 5.4.3 and newer only: 5.4.0, NuttX's default version, counts
           C stack use differently (CSTACKCF) and ignores the macro.
Upstream:  Maybe. Generic and small, but needs the numbers above on a second port.

diff --git a/interpreters/lua/Kconfig b/interpreters/lua/Kconfig
index 418cf8472..9702dad12 100644
--- a/interpreters/lua/Kconfig
+++ b/interpreters/lua/Kconfig
@@ -46,6 +46,17 @@ config INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BIT
 	---help---
 		"Use int and float instead of long and double for Lua numbers."
 
+config INTERPRETERS_LUA_MAXCCALLS
+	int "Maximum nesting of C calls (LUAI_MAXCCALLS)"
+	default 200
+	---help---
+		How deep C calls may nest (pcall in pcall, metamethods, string.gsub
+		callbacks, parser nesting) before Lua raises "C stack overflow".
+		Lua's own default of 200 assumes a stack of 100 KB or more; on a
+		task with a small stack the overflow is not caught and corrupts
+		memory. Roughly: stack size / 500 bytes. Only used by Lua 5.4.3 and
+		newer.
+
 config INTERPRETERS_LUA_PRIORITY
 	int "Lua interpreter priority"
 	default 100
diff --git a/interpreters/lua/Makefile b/interpreters/lua/Makefile
index 40daf76ed..bb1eda317 100644
--- a/interpreters/lua/Makefile
+++ b/interpreters/lua/Makefile
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@ ifeq ($(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BITS),y)
 CFLAGS += -DLUA_32BITS
 endif
 
+CFLAGS += -DLUAI_MAXCCALLS=$(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_MAXCCALLS)
+
 ifneq ($(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_PATH),"")
 CFLAGS += -DLUA_PATH_DEFAULT=\"$(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_PATH)\"
 endif
